#{[{:activity/course {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186046659} :activity/first-step {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186481751} :activity/id #uuid "6101ed73-13ea-5145-b8b3-d79477764212" :activity/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186481684 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186425001 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8cec96a9-0200-560d-b96c-38c90ea667a8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -4 & \\frac{1}{8} \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186424995} {:answer/id #uuid "8fae7340-6e28-5c68-b320-f02b1b9ec60a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -\\frac{1}{4} & 8 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186424996} {:answer/id #uuid "c36b4bbc-e8a1-5d32-8dfe-7790ebbd7295" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -\\frac{1}{8} & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186424997} {:answer/id #uuid "d5e47ff6-28fb-5454-9b4c-76a088f298a8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -4 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & \\frac{1}{8} & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186424998} {:answer/id #uuid "fa0af12f-c969-5d5b-9aea-d2eb372f1847" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -\\frac{1}{4} & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 8 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186424999}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186424999} :answer-field/id #uuid "61441954-c7fc-5ef0-9a6b-24fb2c47909b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186425000}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "6c923c04-595e-5b89-9e36-615f924682f7" :question/math-academy-id "q-135398" :question/problem "Find the inverse of the following matrix:\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & \\frac{1}{4} & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -8 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Notice that we're given a Frobenius matrix:\n\n- all entries on the main diagonal are ones\n\n- the matrix has only one column (the $2$nd column) where some entries below the main diagonal are not zeros\n\n- all the other entries outside the main diagonal are zeros\n\nTo find the inverse of a Frobenius matrix, we simply take the non-zero entries outside the main diagonal with opposite signs. \n\nIn our case, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{-1}={[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & \\frac{1}{4} & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -8 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]}^{-1}=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -\\frac{1}{4} & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 8 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "1f75121a-9df3-563e-8541-407684d3fd8f" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186481730}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186481690 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186265736 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "11da6c8b-9969-5900-9b7a-9809072650d3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "6x+2y-3z-12w+12=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263165} {:answer/id #uuid "65aca46c-892b-57cc-bbda-306a11d68a0b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "x-y+z-4w+12=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263880} {:answer/id #uuid "b4fbfa20-0a93-5e20-ad08-85bb7ababd04" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2x-z-8w+18=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264558} {:answer/id #uuid "bdd3eeee-85c8-5935-bbbf-97214b8aff26" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "3x-y-2z-4w+22=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264650} {:answer/id #uuid "df92e64a-c76e-5206-b481-adf89451351c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "6x-y-2z+6w-1=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264941}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186263165} :answer-field/id #uuid "5a0ebee6-3d61-5917-b532-d12fc16fdb57" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265403}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "ba77fa6c-6a35-5c61-ab53-8720f1df1a35" :question/math-academy-id "q-129476" :question/problem "Find the equation of the tangent hyperplane to the hypersurface $w=\\sqrt{x}+\\sqrt{y}-\\sqrt{z}$ at the point $(1,9,4,2).$" :question/worked-solution "The Cartesian equation of the tangent plane to the hypersurface $w=f(x,y,z)$ at the point $({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0},{w}_{0})$ on the hypersurface can be written as\n\n$$\nw-{w}_{0}=(x-{x}_{0})\\frac{∂f}{∂x}({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})+(y-{y}_{0})\\frac{∂f}{∂y}({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})+(z-{z}_{0})\\frac{∂f}{∂z}({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0}).\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\sqrt{x}+\\sqrt{y}-\\sqrt{z})=\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{x}} \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(\\sqrt{x}+\\sqrt{y}-\\sqrt{z})=\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{y}} \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂z} & =\\frac{∂}{∂z}(\\sqrt{x}+\\sqrt{y}-\\sqrt{z})=-\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{z}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we evaluate the partial derivatives at $(x,y,z)=(1,9,4):$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x}(1,9,4) & =\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{1}}=\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂y}(1,9,4) & =\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{9}}=\\frac{1}{6} \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂z}(1,9,4) & =-\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{4}}=-\\frac{1}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we write down the equation of the tangent hyperplane:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}w-2 & =(x-1)\\frac{∂f}{∂x}(1,9,4)+(y-9)\\frac{∂f}{∂y}(1,9,4)+(z-4)\\frac{∂f}{∂z}(1,9,4) \\\\ w-2 & =\\frac{1}{2}(x-1)+\\frac{1}{6}(y-9)-\\frac{1}{4}(z-4) \\\\ w-2 & =\\frac{1}{2}x+\\frac{1}{6}y-\\frac{1}{4}z-1 \\\\ \\frac{1}{2}x+\\frac{1}{6}y-\\frac{1}{4}z-w+1 & =0 \\\\ 12(\\frac{1}{2}x+\\frac{1}{6}y-\\frac{1}{4}z-w+1) & =12\\cdot 0 \\\\ 6x+2y-3z-12w+12 & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "47a1f329-4e6b-541e-a75c-6bd8fee85055" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186481720}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186481711 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186387908 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6770c6c3-ca44-5901-927f-1f6eb9c2f483" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "⟨-1,-\\frac{t}{2+{t}^{2}},0⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387910} {:answer/id #uuid "d6f467ee-f10f-5e09-b08f-f8641934f5aa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "⟨-\\frac{1}{{t}^{2}},-\\frac{{t}^{2}}{1+{t}^{2}},0⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387911} {:answer/id #uuid "375265a8-c029-5e99-9d9a-45d5e93a7d32" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "⟨1,-\\frac{1}{t+{t}^{2}},0⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387912} {:answer/id #uuid "78262439-79b2-52fc-a07a-ed5fa9d567e8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "⟨\\frac{1}{t},-\\frac{1}{t+{t}^{2}},0⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387913} {:answer/id #uuid "b4369e5c-dffe-55df-9352-d2f0194bfc84" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "⟨1,-\\frac{t}{1+{t}^{2}},0⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387914}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186387912} :answer-field/id #uuid "c8592051-0273-5e7f-9289-65035199769c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387909}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "00ec801b-e22a-5c19-899f-45b6911ab4a7" :question/math-academy-id "q-128570" :question/problem "If $g(u)=⟨\\frac{1}{u},\\,\\operatorname{ln}⁡(u+1),\\,1⟩$ and $u(t)=\\frac{1}{t}$, then $(g∘u)^{′}(t)=$" :question/worked-solution "By the chain rule, we have \n\n$$\n(g∘u)^{′}(t)=g′(u(t))u′(t).\n$$\n\nNow, let's find the derivatives of each function:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{g}^{′}(u) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}u}(\\frac{1}{u}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}u}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(u+1)),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}u}(1)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-\\frac{1}{{u}^{2}},\\,\\frac{1}{u+1},\\,0⟩ \\\\ {u}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\frac{1}{t})=-\\frac{1}{{t}^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(g∘u)^{′}(t) & =g′(u(t))u′(t) \\\\  & =⟨-\\frac{1}{(u(t))^{2}},\\,\\frac{1}{u(t)+1},\\,0⟩\\cdot {u}^{′}(t) \\\\  & =⟨-{t}^{2},\\,\\frac{t}{1+t},\\,0⟩\\cdot (-\\frac{1}{{t}^{2}}) \\\\  & =⟨1,-\\frac{1}{t+{t}^{2}},0⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "72e28279-670b-5a89-8400-cd558e3d146a"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186481712 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186476898 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "27c5aab8-0a81-5132-a7be-619ec038e1a5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "A leftward-opening parabola with a vertex at $(-2,0)$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186476292} {:answer/id #uuid "2c4674c7-f259-581e-8614-736a3cb60f3d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "A downward-opening parabola with a vertex at $(-2,0)$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186476303} {:answer/id #uuid "5d59a046-342f-501f-ac16-73130a0b65f9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "A leftward-opening parabola with a vertex at $(0,-2)$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186476412} {:answer/id #uuid "850ca197-95db-57a6-9657-7a8c734bb035" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{R}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186476493} {:answer/id #uuid "b3492ae0-c5c3-5f74-a048-e9fe9d78ac1a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "A downward-opening parabola with a vertex at $(0,-2)$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186476609}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186476412} :answer-field/id #uuid "85d8478a-9dda-5ec1-b44a-27ba892935a0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186476815}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "52ee82cc-593c-5df5-9ddf-f0c4aabcb195" :question/math-academy-id "q-164421" :question/problem "What is the domain in the $xy$-plane of the parabolic cylinder $(y+2)^{2}=-4x?$" :question/worked-solution "The full expression describing all points on our parabolic cylinder is\n\n$$\n(y+2)^{2}=-4x,\\,z=k\n$$\n\nwhere $k\\in R$ can vary arbitrarily. \n\nThe domain of any cylinder in the $xy$-plane is its base curve. Hence, in this case, the domain is\n\n$$\n\\{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}:(y+2)^{2}=-4x\\}.\n$$\n\nThis is a leftward-opening parabola with a vertex at $(0,-2).$"} :step/id #uuid "7814611f-bd6e-5ef0-bcdc-00eabc6313cf" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186481690}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186481720 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186250244 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "353c38c6-0699-5d31-a3a7-681d96b0021d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247901} {:answer/id #uuid "5507088f-1a8b-5d15-a203-9e83009f5db2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248191} {:answer/id #uuid "85d825e8-4b77-570d-9579-44732d982d72" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-\\frac{2}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248617} {:answer/id #uuid "c26ec3ba-1125-5219-b27d-d1384ee85f70" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-\\frac{6}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249151} {:answer/id #uuid "d210b2f5-3730-5d88-a77c-6afcdc80ecd9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249287}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186248617} :answer-field/id #uuid "e7cbe6e3-ee8a-56d6-bba3-4dcd2dab931c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186250069}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "0ba270d9-6da5-5830-bec9-26eadbb91904" :question/math-academy-id "q-114330" :question/problem "${\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /5}5x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x)\\,\\text{d}x=$" :question/worked-solution "Let's use integration by parts. We set\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=5x & ⇒ & {u}^{′}=5 \\\\ {v}^{′}=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x) & ⇒ & v=\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5x)}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into the integration by parts formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x & =uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int 5x\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x)\\,\\text{d}x & =5x\\cdot \\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5x)}{5}-\\int \\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5x)}{5}\\cdot 5\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5x)-\\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡(5x)\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate the integral and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /5}5x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x)\\,\\text{d}x & =x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5x){|}_{0}^{\\pi /5}-{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /5}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5x){|}_{0}^{\\pi /5}+\\frac{1}{5}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x){|}_{0}^{\\pi /5} \\\\  & =[\\frac{\\pi }{5}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{5})-0\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5\\cdot 0)] \\\\  & +\\frac{1}{5}[\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{5})-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5\\cdot 0)] \\\\  & =(0-0)+\\frac{1}{5}(-1-1) \\\\  & =-\\frac{2}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "8cbf31c4-5f52-5b80-a380-3e406c5a51de" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186481684}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186481730 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186354530 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "14078cbb-e2f9-5c26-80b6-ce16aa62ca33" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451869} {:answer/id #uuid "618b19c8-3470-50fe-b37b-4cc4086849aa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451870}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186451869} :answer-field/id #uuid "dd4d02ca-f845-54bf-97b7-803e44eb3ff2" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452782} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d62be857-de11-55f2-bf65-a6f6fa2b4ed2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451871} {:answer/id #uuid "63d3abf6-f57f-54e2-a190-75a48dc84fa1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451872}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186451871} :answer-field/id #uuid "eebb9ca8-6ae2-54a4-8b8d-d24fe6daf795" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452783} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d54569e8-25cd-51fb-9e4c-cbeb92e1913c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451873} {:answer/id #uuid "4a739055-caf5-5dad-a093-92704b147e1d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451874}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186451874} :answer-field/id #uuid "edc906f1-6059-5fa6-9455-d997269a94cd" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452784}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "020f4792-4587-5aa1-be12-a9175f71b2e8" :question/math-academy-id "q-86867" :question/problem "Let $D$ be a finite region enclosed by the curve $\\frac{{x}^{2}}{9}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{4}=1.$ If \n\n$$\nf(x,y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}{e}^{x-y}, & (x,y)\\in R\\cap D \\\\ 0, & (x,y)\\in R∖D,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \nwhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** ${∬}_{D}{e}^{x-y}\\,\\text{d}A={∬}_{R}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A,\\,$ where $R=[-2,2]\\times [-3,3]$\n\n- **II.** ${∬}_{R}{e}^{x-y}\\,\\text{d}A={∬}_{D}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A,\\,$ where $R=[-2,2]\\times [-3,3]$\n\n- **III.** ${∬}_{D}{e}^{x-y}\\,\\text{d}A={∬}_{R}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A,\\,$ where $R=[-3,3]\\times [-2,2]$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's draw our region $D:$\n\n![](images/62/62925844de27c9731b181f17a1bdd912bfa3265176bd62ebda425d182ae8d9e8.png)\n\nNotice that if $R$ covers $D$ completely and we define \n\n$$\nf(x,y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}{e}^{x-y}, & (x,y)\\in R\\cap D \\\\ 0, & (x,y)\\in R∖D,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwe obtain\n\n$$\n{∬}_{D}{e}^{x-y}\\,\\text{d}A={∬}_{R}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each of the given statements.\n\n- Statement I is false. The rectangle $R$ does not completely cover the region $D.$\n\n- Statement II is false. The rectangle $R$ does not cover the region $D.$ Also, the integrals have not been stated correctly with respect to the domains $R$ and $D$ (they have been swapped).\n\n- Statement III is true. Indeed, the rectangle $R$ covers the region $D$ completely.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only.\""} :step/id #uuid "b78e0e64-451d-5e76-9ebd-6c7fc97e6aa4" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186481711}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186481751 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186243958 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7c2c12e0-1cd2-57dc-bb2e-fccfbfe29b6c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$1\\cdot f\\ne f$ for some $f\\in F$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186242269} {:answer/id #uuid "aed90e2c-7d1b-5ac3-9ce4-8c895e1d0385" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "addition and scalar multiplication of functions in $F$ do not satisfy the distributive laws" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186242706} {:answer/id #uuid "c9bc4983-8538-5113-9d78-363014648f95" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "addition of $f,g\\in F$ is not commutative" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186242959} {:answer/id #uuid "cdb145c6-2092-56d4-9ff1-6bbe59e69ca7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "addition of $f,g\\in F$ is not associative" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186242990} {:answer/id #uuid "d3235266-f3fb-58a4-8cd7-6dda3548ef28" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$F$ does not contain the zero element" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186243041}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186243041} :answer-field/id #uuid "39664c8c-a6d4-545a-b91d-30b8ab061a3a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186243548}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "fe3a1a04-348a-505c-9183-5288567e7407" :question/math-academy-id "q-106813" :question/problem "Let $F$ be the set of functions $f:R\\to R$ such that $f(0)=\\frac{1}{2}.$ Complete the following sentence:\n\n*$F$ is **not** a vector space (with respect to function addition and scalar multiplication of a function by a real number) because $\\text{_________}\\,.$*" :question/worked-solution "The correct answer is as follows:\n\n*$F$ is **not** a vector space (with respect to function addition and scalar multiplication of a function by a real number) because **$F$ does not contain the zero element.** *\n\nIndeed, evaluating the zero function $f(x)=0$ at $x=0,$ we have $f(0)=0\\ne \\frac{1}{2}.$\n\nOn the other hand:\n\n- Addition of $f,g\\in F$ is associative. $\\,✓$\n\n- Addition of $f,g\\in F$ is commutative. $\\,✓$\n\n- $1\\cdot f=f$ for all $f\\in F.$ $\\,✓$\n\n- Addition and scalar multiplication of functions satisfy the distributive laws. $\\,✓$"} :step/id #uuid "fb46dea9-0a88-5b6c-8caf-f59892237216" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186481712}}] :activity/title "Quiz 11" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045460 :db/ident :activity.type/assessment} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186481573}]}
